{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Python 3 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++14 code to Python 3 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++14 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\nint MOD;\nint mpow(int x, int n) {\n\tint res = 1;\n\twhile (n) {\n\t\tif (n & 1) res = 1LL * res * x % MOD;\n\t\tx = 1LL * x * x % MOD;\n\t\tn >>= 1;\n\t}\n\treturn res;\n}\nconst int N = 3e5 + 5;\nunsigned long long dp[27][N];\nint rf[N], f[N];\nint permute(int n, int m) {\n\treturn 1LL * f[n] * rf[n - m] % MOD;\n}\nint main() {\n\tint n, K;\n\tscanf(\"%d%d%d\", &n, &K, &MOD);\n\tif (n & 1) {\n\t\tprintf(\"%d\\n\", mpow(K, n));\n\t\treturn 0;\n\t}\n\tf[0] = 1;\n\tfor (int i = 1; i <= n; ++ i) f[i] = 1LL * f[i - 1] * i % MOD;\n\trf[n] = mpow(f[n], MOD - 2);\n\tfor (int i = n - 1; i >= 0; -- i) rf[i] = 1LL * rf[i + 1] * (i + 1) % MOD;\n\tdp[0][0] = 1;\n\tfor (int k = 0; k < K; ++ k) {\n\t\tfor (int i = 1; i <= n; ++ i) {\n\t\t\tif ((i & n) != i) continue;\n\t\t\tint cnt = 0;\n\t\t\tunsigned long long &res = dp[k + 1][i];\n\t\t\tint hb = 1;\n\t\t\tfor (int t = i; t > 1; t >>= 1) hb <<= 1;\n\t\t\tfor (int j = i - hb; j >= 0; j = (j - 1) & i) {\n\t\t\t\tint jj = j + hb;\n\t\t\t\tres += dp[k][i ^ jj] * rf[jj];\n\t\t\t\tif (cnt ++ == 17) {\n\t\t\t\t\tres %= MOD;\n\t\t\t\t\tcnt = 0;\n\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\tif (j == 0) break;\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\tres %= MOD;\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\tint ans = 0;\n\tfor (int i = 0; i <= K; ++ i) (ans += 1LL * f[n] * dp[i][n] % MOD * permute(K, i) % MOD) %= MOD;\n\tprintf(\"%d\\n\", (mpow(K, n) + MOD - ans) % MOD);\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport sys\n\ndef mpow(x, n, MOD):\n    res = 1\n    while n:\n        if n & 1:\n            res = (res * x) % MOD\n        x = (x * x) % MOD\n        n >>= 1\n    return res\n\ndef main():\n    data = sys.stdin.readline().split()\n    n = int(data[0])\n    K = int(data[1])\n    MOD = int(data[2])\n    \n    if n & 1:\n        print(mpow(K, n, MOD))\n        return\n    \n    f = [0] * (n + 1)\n    rf = [0] * (n + 1)\n    \n    f[0] = 1\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        f[i] = (f[i - 1] * i) % MOD\n    \n    rf[n] = mpow(f[n], MOD - 2, MOD)\n    for i in range(n - 1, -1, -1):\n        rf[i] = (rf[i + 1] * (i + 1)) % MOD\n    \n    # dp[k][i] for k in range(0, K+1) and i in range(0, n+1)\n    dp = [[0] * (n + 1) for _ in range(K + 2)]\n    dp[0][0] = 1\n    \n    for k in range(K):\n        for i in range(1, n + 1):\n            if (i & n) != i:\n                continue\n            res = 0\n            cnt = 0\n            # Find highest bit in i\n            hb = 1\n            t = i\n            while t > 1:\n                hb <<= 1\n                t >>= 1\n            j = i - hb\n            while True:\n                jj = j + hb\n                res += dp[k][i ^ jj] * rf[jj]\n                cnt += 1\n                if cnt == 18:\n                    res %= MOD\n                    cnt = 0\n                if j == 0:\n                    break\n                j = (j - 1) & i\n            dp[k + 1][i] = res % MOD\n    \n    ans = 0\n    for i in range(K + 1):\n        perm = (f[n] * rf[n - i]) % MOD if n >= i else 0\n        term = (f[n] * dp[i][n]) % MOD\n        term = (term * perm) % MOD\n        term = (term * mpow(K, i, MOD)) % MOD  # permute(K, i) = K!/(K-i)! but here we need K*(K-1)*...*(K-i+1)\n        # Actually permute(K, i) = K!/(K-i)! = f[K] * rf[K-i] but K can be large, so we compute directly\n        # Let's recompute permute(K, i) properly\n        perm_val = 1\n        for j in range(i):\n            perm_val = (perm_val * (K - j)) % MOD\n        term = (f[n] * dp[i][n]) % MOD\n        term = (term * perm_val) % MOD\n        ans = (ans + term) % MOD\n    \n    result = (mpow(K, n, MOD) + MOD - ans) % MOD\n    print(result)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.75\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-0.00024303820100612938, -9.536738616588991e-07, -3.576278118089249e-07, -0.14435243606567383, -0.000161038784426637, -0.00017796363681554794, -0.006762949284166098, -0.20556692779064178, -1.7165990357170813e-05, -4.291525328881107e-06, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.011053166352212429, -0.0009566736407577991, -7.629365427419543e-06, -4.529942543740617e-06, -2.253030106658116e-05, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, -8.344646857949556e-07, 0.0, -0.03804657980799675, 0.0, -3.6954811548639555e-06, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -1.1920922133867862e-06, -1.1920928244535389e-07, 0.0, 0.0, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -5.960446742392378e-06, -1.1920928244535389e-07, 0.0, -0.1270786076784134, -0.00014149141497910023, 0.0, -4.768370445162873e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, 0.0, -9.536697689327411e-06, -1.6689286894688848e-06, -1.645074735279195e-05, 0.0, 0.0, -3.576278118089249e-07, 0.0, -1.1920928244535389e-07, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, -8.34461570775602e-06, -3.576278118089249e-07, -2.276871418871451e-05, 0.0, -1.1920922133867862e-06, 0.0, -1.0728830375228426e-06, -3.576278118089249e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -9.536738616588991e-07, -1.0728830375228426e-06, -1.0013530300057027e-05, -0.00010883215873036534, -0.00639